# {{ name | kebab_case }}

A NATS server with JetStream, generated by the `bus` Moon template. It carries
the events the APIs send each other (an Axum API generated with `--events`
writes them to an outbox in its own database and relays them here).

```bash
moon run {{ name | kebab_case }}:up      # start it
moon run {{ name | kebab_case }}:down    # stop it, keeping the data
```

It listens on `127.0.0.1:{{ port }}` (`PORT` in `.env.example`; Moon checks it
against the other services' ports) and keeps its streams in a Docker volume
named after this repository folder. `docker compose down -v` in this folder
deletes them.

An API reads the address from `NATS_URL` in its `.env`; the example file has the
local one.

## Production

Run a NATS cluster with JetStream (three servers, `replicas: 3` on the streams)
and TLS, and give each API its own credentials. The API connects to whatever
`NATS_URL` says, so nothing in the code changes.
